% ============================================================================
% ocean-current-strongest-location.query.adj — worked recall over the
% ocean-current-strongest-location library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "where are tidal
% currents strongest?" (direct) or "which current type is strongest near
% the shore and in bays and estuaries?" (reverse) — it states no fact of
% its own — it only `import`s the grounded table and asks binding
% queries. A current type that is not the one tabled here abstains
% honestly — the engine never invents a location.
% ============================================================================

import "ocean-current-strongest-location.adj"

? ocean_current_strongest_location(tidal_currents, $Location)                                                        % expect near_the_shore_and_in_bays_and_estuaries_along_the_coast
? ocean_current_strongest_location($CurrentType, near_the_shore_and_in_bays_and_estuaries_along_the_coast)           % reverse bind — expect tidal_currents
? ocean_current_strongest_location(thermohaline_circulation, $Location)                                              % expect abstain -- the cited thermohaline span names no location
